1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,478
This is the last lecture of the class,

2
00:00:03,928 --> 00:00:06,972
and there's almost nothing new in it.

3
00:00:08,772 --> 00:00:13,989
Everything you've written since Lecture one is about to become one episode.

4
00:00:14,889 --> 00:00:17,933
It has a beginning at the station,

5
00:00:18,383 --> 00:00:20,557
a middle inside the ruin,

6
00:00:21,007 --> 00:00:23,180
and an ending back home.

7
00:00:24,080 --> 00:00:30,167
And today you learn to check it, from the first line to the last.

8
00:00:31,367 --> 00:00:35,280
Before I change anything, I read what I have.

9
00:00:36,180 --> 00:00:38,789
This table is the whole episode.

10
00:00:39,689 --> 00:00:42,298
Each row is something that happens.

11
00:00:42,748 --> 00:00:46,226
It says where it happens, who does it,

12
00:00:46,676 --> 00:00:48,415
and what finishes it.

13
00:00:50,215 --> 00:00:53,259
Seven of the rows are the story,

14
00:00:53,709 --> 00:00:58,057
and the game is won when those seven are done.

15
00:00:58,957 --> 00:01:04,174
The other five are what a curious crew finds on the way.

16
00:01:05,974 --> 00:01:10,322
Draw a table like this for every episode you write.

17
00:01:10,772 --> 00:01:13,380
Draw it first, before any record.

18
00:01:14,280 --> 00:01:17,324
Every row needs something that finishes it,

19
00:01:17,774 --> 00:01:19,948
and somebody who's able to.

20
00:01:21,148 --> 00:01:25,061
Last time the mast was a quest by itself.

21
00:01:25,961 --> 00:01:28,135
Now it opens the episode.

22
00:01:29,935 --> 00:01:32,109
So I delete that quest,

23
00:01:32,559 --> 00:01:37,341
and I type it again inside the arc, with four hashes.

24
00:01:38,241 --> 00:01:40,415
It gets three more lines:

25
00:01:40,865 --> 00:01:43,909
a Then, to reveal the next step,

26
00:01:44,359 --> 00:01:48,707
and the two lines that make it count toward winning.

27
00:01:49,607 --> 00:01:53,954
The lead line and the list stay as they were.

28
00:01:54,404 --> 00:01:56,578
Only the middle paragraph changes,

29
00:01:57,028 --> 00:02:00,072
to say why the mast comes first.

30
00:02:01,872 --> 00:02:05,350
And the way in is no longer first,

31
00:02:05,800 --> 00:02:08,409
so it starts when it's revealed.

32
00:02:09,609 --> 00:02:12,652
Earlier the ship got a clue chain.

33
00:02:13,102 --> 00:02:14,841
Comms logged some names,

34
00:02:15,291 --> 00:02:18,770
and a later call had one more answer.

35
00:02:20,570 --> 00:02:24,917
This is the same idea, for somebody in a suit.

36
00:02:25,817 --> 00:02:29,730
At the altar, the answer that reads the marks

37
00:02:30,180 --> 00:02:33,659
now learns a fact, and starts a quest.

38
00:02:34,559 --> 00:02:37,167
The quest has a small table,

39
00:02:37,617 --> 00:02:40,661
what the crew knows about the marks.

40
00:02:41,561 --> 00:02:45,039
It gives them the number without the answer.

41
00:02:45,939 --> 00:02:49,852
Then the cairn gets a scene of its own.

42
00:02:50,752 --> 00:02:55,535
And one of its answers says if learned, at least one.

43
00:02:57,335 --> 00:03:03,422
So a crew member who read the marks can count the stones against them.

44
00:03:03,872 --> 00:03:07,785
One who didn't just sees a pile of stones.

45
00:03:08,685 --> 00:03:13,033
And the count sends the word that finishes the quest.

46
00:03:14,233 --> 00:03:16,841
I run lint, and it's clean.

47
00:03:17,741 --> 00:03:20,785
I misspell the quest on the answer,

48
00:03:21,235 --> 00:03:23,409
and lint names the line.

49
00:03:25,209 --> 00:03:27,817
But lint only reads a file.

50
00:03:28,267 --> 00:03:30,441
It can't play an episode.

51
00:03:31,341 --> 00:03:34,820
So the last check isn't lint at all.

52
00:03:36,020 --> 00:03:38,628
The last check is a walk.

53
00:03:39,528 --> 00:03:42,572
Every row of the episode, in order,

54
00:03:43,022 --> 00:03:46,935
with what I expect written down before I start.

55
00:03:48,735 --> 00:03:53,517
In row one, the quest list has one step, the mast.

56
00:03:54,417 --> 00:03:59,200
In row two, near the station, the app offers the worksite.

57
00:04:00,100 --> 00:04:03,143
I go out, I weld the mast,

58
00:04:03,593 --> 00:04:05,767
and the next step appears.

59
00:04:06,667 --> 00:04:10,580
I've got forty credits, and the table says forty.

60
00:04:12,380 --> 00:04:16,293
Then I come aboard and fly to the door.

61
00:04:16,743 --> 00:04:19,787
Ninety credits, and the table says ninety.

62
00:04:20,987 --> 00:04:26,639
Now I suit up again, and this time the app names the Hollow.

63
00:04:28,439 --> 00:04:31,483
At the ring, Comms logs the names.

64
00:04:32,383 --> 00:04:35,426
At the altar the step is done,

65
00:04:35,876 --> 00:04:39,354
and I read the marks on the rim.

66
00:04:40,254 --> 00:04:43,298
There's the new quest in the list.

67
00:04:45,098 --> 00:04:47,707
Comms plays the entry for Dace,

68
00:04:48,157 --> 00:04:51,635
and marks the side room and the Gallery.

69
00:04:52,535 --> 00:04:55,578
At the cairn, the side story finishes,

70
00:04:56,028 --> 00:04:59,507
and the cutscene plays on the main screen.

71
00:05:00,407 --> 00:05:04,320
And on my suit, there's the answer I earned.

72
00:05:05,220 --> 00:05:06,959
I count the stones,

73
00:05:07,409 --> 00:05:09,148
and there are forty-one.

74
00:05:10,348 --> 00:05:13,826
Then the slab, twelve seconds with the beam.

75
00:05:14,726 --> 00:05:16,465
Then it's the niche.

76
00:05:16,915 --> 00:05:20,393
Comms opens it, and I take the bowl.

77
00:05:22,193 --> 00:05:25,237
I come aboard, and we fly home.

78
00:05:26,137 --> 00:05:28,311
Eight hundred and twenty credits,

79
00:05:28,761 --> 00:05:32,239
and the table says eight hundred and twenty.

80
00:05:33,139 --> 00:05:34,878
Every row has agreed.

81
00:05:36,678 --> 00:05:39,287
Then I check the other ending.

82
00:05:40,187 --> 00:05:44,970
I set the clock to twenty seconds, and I sit still.

83
00:05:45,420 --> 00:05:47,159
There's my Lose sentence.

84
00:05:48,059 --> 00:05:51,537
And the log file is empty after both.

85
00:05:52,737 --> 00:05:55,780
Here's one more thing before you go.

86
00:05:56,680 --> 00:06:01,028
In Class three you wrote a story for one person.

87
00:06:01,928 --> 00:06:07,146
A ruin can carry one too, in a section of its own,

88
00:06:07,596 --> 00:06:12,813
and the game hands it to the crew member who suits up.

89
00:06:14,613 --> 00:06:17,657
The page shows you one to type,

90
00:06:18,107 --> 00:06:21,150
and it needs no card at all.

91
00:06:22,050 --> 00:06:26,398
Then it lists three things this class hasn't given you,

92
00:06:26,848 --> 00:06:29,891
so you don't go looking for them.

93
00:06:31,091 --> 00:06:33,265
And now the class project.

94
00:06:34,165 --> 00:06:38,948
Make a new mission, and write an episode of your own.

95
00:06:40,748 --> 00:06:42,487
Draw the table first.

96
00:06:43,387 --> 00:06:49,039
Build the ruin, give it a voice, and hide a piece in it.

97
00:06:49,939 --> 00:06:54,722
Write the arc, with a win, a loss and a clock.

98
00:06:56,522 --> 00:06:59,565
Then write your walk, and walk it.

99
00:07:00,465 --> 00:07:05,683
You're finished when your table and your game agree on every row.
